# Who has to approve what.
#
# GitHub silently ignores owners it cannot resolve — a misspelled team or a team
# that does not exist yet yields a CODEOWNERS file that looks strict and enforces
# nothing. Every entry below is a real account today.

# Default owner for everything, including guide content.
*                   @grleblanc

# The security boundary: these decide what content is allowed to exist and how it
# reaches nhmesh.live. Keep them owner-reviewed even after content review is
# delegated to others.
/tools/             @grleblanc
/deploy/            @grleblanc
/.github/           @grleblanc
/sections.json      @grleblanc
/LICENSE            @grleblanc
/SECURITY.md        @grleblanc

# To stop being the only reviewer: create an @NHMesh/kb-maintainers team, add
# trusted contributors, and change the `*` line above to point at it. Leave the
# specific paths on @grleblanc. Adding the team here before it exists would
# quietly disable ownership review entirely.
